window.products.push({"id":366383,"name":"Kaisa Cooling Sheets King, Viscose from Bamboo, 6 Pieces Sheets Set with 16\" Deep Pocket, Soft Breathable Bedding Sets for Hot Sleepers, Silky Hotel K","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":139.99,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61x0v9a2N9L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Viscose from Bamboo: Kaisa king sheets set is organic, OEKO-TEX 100 certified with divine texture of silk, endorsing organic and sustainable living. Combining the benefits of natural green fiber and synthetic fiber, bamboo blend fiber is known for its superior breathability and durability, standing out as a smart, stylish, and safe choice for all. Silk Soft & Breathable: Cozy up to Kaisa cooling bed set to enjoy sublime softness, smoothness, and breathability. Velvety and cool to the touch, viscose from bamboo is hypoallergenic and friendly to the most sensitive skin, so you can dive in its blissful haven to sleep naked and become one with nature. What You Get: Kaisa bed sheets king size come with 1x fitted sheet, 1x flat sheet, and 4x pillowcases for change and clean. 16\" deep pockets of the fitted sheet with periphery elastic fit all high or double mattresses you've already have. Deep Pocket Design: Highest quality fabric with impeccable sewing makes Kaisa cooling sheets the most luxurious bedding ever. Fully hemmed elastics and extra elastic ribbon at each corner grip on the mattress tightly, no bunching up any more. 60*60s braided 1800 thread count bamboo offers 5 star hotel quality sleeping experience in the comfort of your home. Join into Naked Sleeping: Fully machine washable for hassle-free maintenance, tumble dry low. The luxury bed sheet set restores softness and malleability after each wash, never fades with a forever lustrous finish and supple touch. In any case you have any questions related to Kaisa products, feel free to contact us 24/7.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61x0v9a2N9L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Kaisa","source_asin":"B09Q5CDM1L","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-366383","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09Q5CDM1L","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B09Q5CDM1L","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
window.products.push({"id":366384,"name":"Manual Woodworkers & Weavers Collegiate Throw Pillow, 12.5 x 8.5, University of Alabama Roll Tide","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81EhfYPnckL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"From the mountains of North Carolina, manual WW weaves, sews, prints, and develops not just the fabrics, textiles, and beautiful products you'd expect from a Heritage company, they bring you the freshest designs for your home. Although Thomas Lemuel Oates started manual Woodworkers & Weavers in 1932, the story goes back further. The roots of the company can be found in Oates' entrepreneurial spirit. He and his brother used to farm the Mountain areas of Bat cave in Western North Carolina. They would also help their mother find materials for her crafts. The sons began to make wooden whistles, buckets and bird-houses. They would sell their wares along with her crafts to the people from Charlotte that came through in their horse-drawn buggies on the way to the mountains. Later, Thomas worked at the Ashville postcard company. When the depression hit, he lost his job, but it inspired him to go into business and sell crafts, like cornhusk dolls and woven pieces, that were produced by the local women. He had learned about the Wholesale business while working at Ashville. He built a waterwheel to generate electricity at a mill, began making product and opened shop. Over the years, he expanded the company. His son, Lemuel Oates, who would next manage the company, says he worked in the business from a young age. He explains the products were made from cotton scraps left over from making socks. Half-inch circles would be looped together to form a variety of products. Lemuel Oates went to college and then settled in Richmond. In December 1973, he returned to Bat cave and took over the company. In 2007 his son Travis and his daughter, Molly Oates Sherrill, took over the business.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81EhfYPnckL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"MWW","source_asin":"B00I81DLU4","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-366384","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00I81DLU4","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B00I81DLU4","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
